Z||000000||Boomtastic||09-26-2001||07:27 PM||||Okay - we've all seen them, and most of us have experienced them. I'm talking about broken sensor clips!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I've seen MAP sensor connectors held in place with cable ties, and ignition module connectors tied back up with tiny bungee cords (hmmm - wonder who THAT could be?), but other than going back to GM and leaving your wallet on the Parts Counter, your only other source is cutting them off of a good harness and splicing them into the old harness. We all know that looks like dog poop, but sometimes it has to be done. Well, here's where you come in! I've been thinking of supplying OEM connectors for less than GM can, but I have a dilemma. Do people want connectors with pig tails attached, or do they want ones that they can cut the cables and add the terminals to and make an OEM looking connector with NO splicing? Without going into the specifics, I need valid thoughts as to which you would prefer and why. And to answer any questions that people may want to ask: <P>a) I don't know when I'll be offering these.<P>b) Yes, I will do almost every connector in the car, not just the engine, IF there is a call for it. (In some cases I need to purchase 3000 connectors minimum to get a reasonable price, not including the wire, seals, or terminals. That's JUST the black plastic connector housing! If not, the price goes up (for me) approx. 200%)<P>c) Yes, I will cover both engine choices, and maybe more.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>d) Prices. This will depend on the quantity of pieces I buy, the extent to which I assemble them, and various other issues. I'm shooting for around $5 ~ $10 per connector plus shipping, but DO NOT quote me on that. This is all still in the "Beta" stages.<P>Email me directly if you'd like, or post to the forum - you're choice.<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||09-26-2001||07:31 PM||||That would be cool.  I have remade my own weatherpack connectors before and it looks better than pig tails.  But that might not be the best all the time.  Some connectors need to have the pig tails because the wires would be too short to crimp another end onto and still reach the sensor.  So maybe supplying both would be a good idea.  Eitherw way I know I will be ordering some from you when/if you do this! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Boomtastic||09-26-2001||07:35 PM||||My thoughts on the short wires are that you could take apart the old connectors and cut the wires at the terminals. You wouldn't loose very much at all. The new connectors will come with all of the correct silicone weather seals and terminal guides (if applicable). I tested the V6 ignition module connectors today and found that they were a perfect replacement. They only difference is that the color of the seal was blue and not green. No biggie. I'll have a few pics online if anyone wants to see the connectors ...||||reg||14
