Z||000007||Boomtastic||09-26-2001||08:14 PM||||Here's the pictures of the samples and descriptions:<P>2 Wire Connector, from the front<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2_wire_front.jpg"> <P>2 Wire Connector, from the rear<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2_wire_rear.jpg"> <P>4 Wire Connector, from the front<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4_wire_front.jpg"> <P>4 Wire Connector, from the rear<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4_wire_rear.jpg"> <P>4 Wire Connector, exploded view<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4_wire_apart.jpg"> <P>The terminals ("pull to seat" style)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/terminal.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Boomtastic||09-26-2001||08:17 PM||||Here's a closeup of the 4 wire connector. This is the primary difference with these connectors - they have a guide so that people can assemble them and get the terminals inserted correctly the first try.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4_wire_close.jpg"> <P>Installation is also VERY easy:<BR>a) Thread wire through everything in order.<BR>b) Crimp terminal on wire.<BR>c) Pull to seat.<P>Reusing any part is up to the end user's discretion (if they wanted to keep the green seal, they can replace it with their own. All pieces interchange with OEM).||||reg||1
